/*
  Pressure.strings
  TeslaSync — P4 shared surface · 0086 · Pressure (Apple)

  The P1/S10 i18n catalog contribution for this surface. The web source
  (components/data-display/format/Pressure.tsx) renders NO translatable copy: it displays a
  locale-formatted number followed by the user's pressure-unit symbol (`bar` / `psi` / `kPa`, sourced
  from the `useUnits()` preference bag, not this component's copy) and, when no finite value is
  supplied, the em-dash sentinel "—" (a symbol, not prose). The only locale-sensitive visible output is
  the number itself, which is bound through the injected `UnitPreferences.locale` (the native parity of
  the web `fmtNumber` global-locale read), not a string table.

  The lone key below is a native accessibility refinement: the web renders a bare "—" with no
  `aria-label`, so VoiceOver would announce just the dash. The native empty branch voices this
  localized label instead. The per-surface table name ("Pressure") folds into the app
  `Localizable.xcstrings` master catalog at integration time.
*/

/* VoiceOver label for the empty branch (no finite pressure supplied; visible text is "—"). */
"pressure.empty.accessibilityLabel" = "No pressure data";
